    "result_text": "The build is green. All changes are complete and the test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133). The DTO is generated from `openapi.yml`, so I updated the spec and the code that populates/consumes the field:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string enum (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) with `membershipLevel`, an `int32` field constrained `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, documenting the \"level 4 reserved for tenure\" note.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced `toMembershipTier` (returning `\"SILVER\"`/`\"BRONZE\"`) with `toMembershipLevel`, computing: start at 1, +1 when a non-blank email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. Updated the `@Mapping` target accordingly.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Removed the household-based `GOLD` promotion in `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning` (and the now-unused `householdMemberCount` helper and `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_MEMBER_THRESHOLD` constant), since membership level caps at 3 and level 4 is reserved for tenure.\n   - Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` (using the mapper's computed level) instead of implying the old tier.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (owner with email + unique name \u2192 level `1 + 1 + 1 = 3`) passes, along with the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
